{"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"GOV_PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":19720018253,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"d188cb158df041dab36142b07166fb2b","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Structural Mechanics"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":19720018253,"ear":"NO","id":"c24a1043107149aea312fa9f83f2fb44","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-06-17T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","otherReportNumbers":["NASA-TN-D-6850","MSC-S-316","Report Number: NASA-TN-D-6850","Report Number: MSC-S-316"],"fundingNumbers":[{"number":"RTOP 914-13-20-13-72","submissionId":19720018253,"id":"8e1fce47c56a4714968f2a9ce2941fa1","type":"PROJECT"}],"title":"Apollo experience report:  Lunar module landing gear subsystem","stiType":"OTHER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-09-02T16:08:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":19720018253,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Rogers, W. F."},"organization":{"name":"NASA Lyndon B. Johnson Space Center","location":"Houston, TX, United States"}},"id":"f286dc9d26d44a04ab9129feedb7f734"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Other - NASA Technical Note (TN)","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":19720018253,"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":"72N25903"},"created":"2013-09-02T16:08:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"CDMS","name":"Legacy CDMS","id":"092d6e0881874968859b972d39a888dc"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"The development of the lunar module landing gear subsystem through the Apollo 11 lunar landing mission is presented. The landing gear design evolved from the design requirement, which had to satisfy the structural, mechanical, and landing performance constraints of the vehicle. Extensive analyses and tests were undertaken to verify the design adequacy. Techniques of the landing performance analysis served as a primary tool in developing the subsystem hardware and in determining the adequacy of the landing gear for toppling stability and energy absorption. The successful Apollo 11 lunar landing mission provided the first opportunity for a complete flight test of the landing gear under both natural and induced environments.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","publications":[{"submissionId":19720018253,"id":"7597c8babe2d4090a993fdb9bed09dd9","publicationDate":"1972-06-01T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"19720018253.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/19720018253/downloads/19720018253.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/19720018253/downloads/19720018253.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/19720018253/downloads/19720018253.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"}